{"parentUuid":"ea30b557-a843-48c0-bc86-4ce9ef37e3b4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"ae3860a1dc6cbabb8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012npUrU1g9ojGrcTeoMMREz","type":"tool_result","content":"# CPMpy Latest Version Information\n\nThe current latest version of CPMpy is **0.10.0**, released on **January 19, 2026**.\n\n## Recent Release History (Most Recent 5-10 Versions)\n\n| Version | Release Date |\n|---------|--------------|\n| 0.10.0 | Jan 19, 2026 |\n| 0.9.29 | Jan 15, 2026 |\n| 0.9.28 | Oct 17, 2025 |\n| 0.9.27 | Oct 6, 2025 |\n| 0.9.26 | Aug 10, 2025 |\n| 0.9.25 | May 7, 2025 |\n| 0.9.24 | Jan 17, 2025 |\n| 0.9.23 | Oct 8, 2024 |\n| 0.9.22 | Oct 3, 2024 |\n| 0.9.21 | Jul 5, 2024 |\n\nThe library is described as \"a numpy-based library for modeling constraint programming problems\" and maintains an active release schedule with multiple updates throughout the year."}]},"uuid":"ee97ec43-f3e8-4d3c-8a3c-58c01b2ffb98","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:47.517Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea30b557-a843-48c0-bc86-4ce9ef37e3b4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"08fca9c6-809a-44bb-89cc-3bc2c4bc1f0c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"ae3860a1dc6cbabb8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHK5f49WDTP6rHc4Hk66MD","type":"tool_result","content":"# cvc5 PyPI Package Information\n\nThe **current latest version of cvc5 on PyPI is 1.3.4**, which was \"Released: May 7, 2026.\"\n\nBoth version 1.3.4 and 1.3.3 are available. Version 1.3.3 was released on February 25, 2026, making it the previous stable release before the most recent update."}]},"uuid":"58ef5496-e6ac-4a59-ab11-11a5134509ac","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:47.748Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08fca9c6-809a-44bb-89cc-3bc2c4bc1f0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d724ddcf-73d8-4a16-911d-53edef70d15f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"ae3860a1dc6cbabb8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vbiqo5HBEHKZDCjfuy2RoA","type":"tool_result","content":"# CPMpy Release History\n\n## Recent Releases Overview\n\nThe visible releases include versions 0.9.21 through 0.10.0, with the following dates:\n\n- **v0.10.0** - January 19, 2024\n- **v0.9.29** - January 15, 2024\n- **v0.9.28** - October 17, 2023\n- **v0.9.27** - October 6, 2023\n- **v0.9.26** - August 10, 2023\n- **v0.9.25** - May 7, 2023\n- **0.9.24** - January 17, 2023\n- **0.9.23** - October 8, 2022\n- **0.9.22** - October 3, 2022\n- **v0.9.21** - July 5, 2022\n\n## v0.10.0 Release Notes (January 19, 2024)\n\nThis major release introduced several significant enhancements:\n\n**New Solver**: \"RC2 MaxSAT solver\" was added to the toolkit, expanding solver capabilities.\n\n**Enhanced Encoding**: The `to_cnf` transformation was expanded using the \"pindakaas encoding backend\" for more sophisticated constraint-to-normal-form conversions.\n\n**Boolean-Integer Linearization**: A new transformation for \"linearisation of multiplication between Boolean and Integer\" variables was implemented.\n\n**Compatibility Fix**: Support was added for \"newest OR-Tools 9.15 release,\" addressing integration challenges with the updated constraint programming library.\n\nAdditional improvements included solution callbacks for Hexaly, documentation enhancements, and various bug fixes across multiple solver interfaces."}]},"uuid":"3b72ecbb-15f8-465a-b5dd-9c97a863a66c","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:48.867Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d724ddcf-73d8-4a16-911d-53edef70d15f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"43d341a2-5779-4806-b821-d49ab5b5b788","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6fa20b73-a995-4ae4-b928-344e193a8ce4","agentId":"ae3860a1dc6cbabb8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CSUFWwDiVWerc4Aiaf824b","type":"tool_result","content":"# Z3-Solver Latest Version Information\n\n**Current Latest Version:** 4.16.0.0, released February 19, 2026\n\n**Recent Versions with Release Dates:**\n\n- 4.16.0.0 – Feb 19, 2026\n- 4.15.8.0 – Feb 12, 2026\n- 4.15.4.0 – Oct 29, 2025\n- 4.15.3.0 – Aug 16, 2025\n- 4.15.1.0 – Jun 8, 2025\n- 4.15.0.0 – May 10, 2025\n- 4.14.1.0 – Mar 11, 2025\n- 4.14.0.0 – Feb 18, 2025\n\nZ3 is described as \"a theorem prover from Microsoft Research with support for bitvectors, booleans, arrays, floating point numbers, strings, and other data types.\""}]},"uuid":"bd62944a-2192-4ecb-b8e7-450a8e83d4f8","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:50:49.210Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43d341a2-5779-4806-b821-d49ab5b5b788","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
